@startuml purchase-walk
title e2e — one card payment

' Script: e2e/purchase-walk/purchase_walk.py
' The client stands in for a browser. It mints the idempotency key.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
left to right direction

actor "Purchase client" as client

rectangle "Bank" {
  usecase "Pay with a card" as pay
  usecase "Read the purchase" as show
  usecase "Read account balances" as accounts
  usecase "Read the audit trail" as trail
}

client --> accounts
client --> pay
client --> show
client --> trail

note right of pay
  POST /api/purchases
  The client declares Idempotency-Key
  for this attempt (e2e-<uuid>).
  The same key returns the original trail.
  Body: card token and amount.
end note

note right of show
  GET /api/purchases/{purchaseId}
  Hold, clearing item, and settlement.
end note

note right of accounts
  GET /api/ledger/accounts/{code}
  2100 customer, 2200 merchant,
  2300 suspense, 4100 income.
  Read before the payment and after it.
end note

note right of trail
  GET /api/audit?traceId=
  traceId comes back from the payment.
end note

note bottom
  Order: snapshot the four accounts, pay,
  read the purchase, read the accounts again,
  read the audit for that trace.
  The client checks the amount, the fee,
  and the four purchase actions.
end note

@enduml
